{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457645-tremere-council-of-seven-spheres-of-control","id":1457645,"title":"Tremere Council of Seven Spheres of Control","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-25T13:41:04-07:00","id":1457645,"title":"Tremere Council of Seven Spheres of Control","content":"Hello, all.<br /> <br /> I'm back in the saddle here after a long absence, and looking forward to spitballing Vampire ideas once again. At the moment I am updating the Tremere wiki for my Concord of Ashes chronicle and I suddenly realised there was a glaring gap in my knowledge.<br /> <br /> The spheres of oversight for the Council of Seven in the modern nights are well-documented, but so far as I am aware the territories in the Dark Medieval iteration have been left rather more amorphous. Am I mistaken in believing that? With AD 1220 in mind, here is what I can recall:<br /> <br /> Goratrix: The Kingdom of France<br /> Meelinda: The British Isles (and remnants of the Angevin Empire on the continent?)<br /> Abetorius: The Byzantine Remnant and the Levant (and presumably the Turkish Beyliks of Anatolia)<br /> Etrius: &quot;Transylvania and the Surrounding Lands&quot; (I take this to mean the Kingdoms of Hungary, Croatia, and Serbia as well as the lands of Ruthenia, Oltenia, Muntenia, and Lesser Poland)<br /> Xavier de Cincao: The Iberian Peninsula (and the Balearic Islands?)<br /> <br /> The other two councillors have been deliberately left for the Storyteller to decide, but that also leaves the remaining regions of the Dark Medieval up for speculation.<br /> <br /> The Holy Roman Empire is obvious, but what then of Etrius' interest in Vienna/Austria?<br /> <br /> The Italian peninsula seems a logical choice as well.<br /> <br /> But what then of Scandinavia, the Baltic, and the Slavic West and North? I seem to recall that he was less than nostalgic about his Scandinavian heritage, but in Clan Novel Tremere, Etrius clearly has an interest in destroying or bringing to heel the Telyavelic Tremere, perhaps implying that he has a loose oversight over the Baltic at least...<br /> <br /> Does North Africa get a look-in?<br /> <br /> Has anyone here taken a stab at delineating them? I'd love to hear your opinions.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.obsidianportal.com/campaigns/the-concord-of-ashes\" target=\"_blank\">The Concord of Ashes</a>, my Dark Ages Vampire Chronicle","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1790-haligaunt","name":"Haligaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1790_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T13:58:53-07:00","id":1457646,"title":"","content":"North Africa likely has a good number of old hermetic texts, but I'm unsure if the Tremere would value these enough to make a good effort in moving in. If they can control Iberia, which at this point has largely islamicised, it's not a terrible stretch, but I've always felt like the Dark Age Tremere stretched too fast too quickly, and they shouldn't be bothering with backwaters like Britain, nevermind other continents. The Tremere haven't been vampires for 200 years at this point. I like the Tremere, obviously, but... I suppose this recklessness is their character.<br /> <br /> Note: The Tremere aren't going to be opposed to Islam. The issue is purely a matter of logistics and cost/benefit. Assamite Sorcers <i>are </i>going to be opposed to Islam. So really the Tremere have a lot of room to be the magical powerhouse of the Islamic world, as their style is really accommodating/inoffensive/doesn't look like witchcraft, but erudite wizardry, and thus doesn't conflict with the religion for the most part. Infact the Tremere have an Advantage here in that their rivals are more oppressed. <br /> <br /> <br /> Scandinavia is a terrible place for Vampires. Too light during summer. The Baltics aren't great either. They're also not rich lands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-25-2021, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T14:20:06-07:00","id":1457647,"title":"","content":"I don't see how Tremere's magic, rituals and practices wouldn't clash with islamic customs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T14:21:39-07:00","id":1457648,"title":"","content":"I think the Tremere would be operating (or would want to operate) pretty much wherever the Hermetic mages of Europe previously operated, and slowly expanding from that.<br /> <br /> Therefore, as inspiration I would use the original Tribunals from Ars Magica and slot them in wherever possible. (Here is one such <a href=\"https://arsmagica.fandom.com/wiki/Tribunal\" target=\"_blank\">list</a>.) These would then change over time as Tremere influence expands and rivalries between the Councilars are settled. By the modern day, the old Tribunal geography would be completely obsolete. But I think that is how the Tremere would begin given their back story in Ars Magica. They would be familiar with the Tribunal system, and their mortal house would already be using it. I think that is how they would start. They would just need to combine them to get to a system of seven regions.<br /> <br /> Using the existing Councilar areas as a starting point, I think this is how things would be:<br /> <br /> Goratrix - &quot;France&quot; likely corresponds to the Tribunals of Normandy and Provencal (Flanders, Burgundy, southern France, the Pyrenees, Provence, Vasconia and western Lombardy).<br /> <br /> Meerlinda - The British Isles would include the old Tribunals of Stonehenge, Loch Legean, and Hibernia which is pretty much what you would expect with the British Isles.<br /> <br /> Abetorius - This would be the Tribunals of Thebes and Levant (corresponding to the possessions of the Byzantine Empire around 800, excluding Italy but including the rest of its European possessions, Asia Minor, the Holy Land &amp; the crusader Kingdoms, the Levant and Egypt).<br /> <br /> Etrius - The Transylvanian Tribunal (non-Byzantine southeastern Europe, Hungary, Bulgaria and Serb and Croat lands).<br /> <br /> Xavier - Iberia corresponds to the Iberian Tribunal which is both Christian and Muslim Spain. I would also think it includes the Roman Tribunal which includes Italy south of the HRE, Sicily, Sardinia and Corsica, and the Maghreb. This makes for a compact Mediterranean area.<br /> <br /> So what is leftover? They would be the Tribunals of the Rhine, Greater Alps, and Novgorod.<br /> <br /> A combination of the Rhine and Alps would make the most sense. That covers the HRE more or less. It includes the Rhine valley and the Holy Roman Empire north of the Alps, the Alps, including Austria, parts of Bavaria and parts of northern Italy.<br /> <br /> That leaves the Tribunal of Novgorod as its own thing. This would include Poland, Kievan Rus, and Scandinavia.<br /> <br /> The geographic areas do not necessarily map to importance. Despite the relatively large size of &quot;Novgorod&quot;, the Tremere likely have very few houses and vampires in this region. Etrius only has &quot;Transylvania&quot; but that includes a lot of the clan's chantries and members.<br /> <br /> As time goes on and things change, the Council of Seven would begin to depart from this system. And even much earlier it is possible that major sections would change as Councilars fall in and out of favor, and the priorities of Tremere change. But for 1220, I think it's a good, solid starting point, and if you make any divergences have it make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 08-27-2021, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T14:48:08-07:00","id":1457650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457645-tremere-council-of-seven-spheres-of-control?p=1457647#post1457647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how Tremere's magic, rituals and practices wouldn't clash with islamic customs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not an expert, but I believe at this time Islam was quite tolerant during this period. Often it's the case that if you aren't muslim, they'll leave you and your religious practices alone (so long as you pay more tax) <br /> <br /> As for attitudes to magic, there is a real bias. People that make contact with spirits and such? That's Evil and must be punished. But using the stars, alchemy, or other non-blasphemous methods? That's just making use of God's creation. The Tremere really have the most compatible paradigm, and they would really benefit from embracing non-strict muslims. Hermeticism requires some faith but it also requires some flexibility, and for that, the Islamic world at this time is no worse than the Christian one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T16:00:21-07:00","id":1457655,"title":"","content":"Both Christians and Muslims revere King Solomon who was also known to be a mighty wizard because of the wisdom granted to him by god. He had control over spirits and demons. Solomonic magic was therefore acceptable magic to the Abrahamic faith, and formed the basis for some of Hermetic magic. I don't see any reason why the Tremere could not fit within Muslim society any less than they could in Christian society of the time. If you can buy into there being an organization like the Order of Hermes in Europe, then a similar enough group can fit into the Muslim world as well. <br /> <br /> And Islam has just as much of a Greek inheritance through their conquests in the Middle East and Africa as does Christianity even if it developed a different way. In so far as European Hermetics developed their knowledge through ancient texts, those texts would have predominantly come to them through transmission from Islam in Spain as there were enough Europeans who knew Arabic in Spain who could translate the texts into Latin while the original Greek was mostly unknown to western Europeans until much later. The Pope Sylvester II was accorded to have magical powers precisely because of the knowledge he learned in Cordoba at Spain. He was supposed to have had a book of spells he obtained from an Arab philosopher from Spain.<br /> <br /> I think the Tremere could easily disguise themselves and find recruits in the Muslim world. It shouldn't be any more difficult than in Europe. Since the Muslim world at this time was probably more literate and educated than Europe, they might have even more success. We should also remember that belief in high magic, astrology, and such did not mark someone as superstitious or ignorant at this time, but educated. It's really a matter of whether such magic can be portrayed as being acceptable to God or in defiance of him. The wrong kind of magic would get you killed. The right kind was OK. Now as vampires, the Tremere would be hunted and killed in the Muslim world just like they were in Europe. That's why you have the Masquerade/Silence of the Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T16:52:24-07:00","id":1457660,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the notion of <i>sorcery</i> (blasphemous magic, so to speak) only became really broad far later, and even then it began in earnest among Christianity. Muslims and Jews were far more tolerant towards mysticism until about the mid-20th century.<br /> <br /> And it helps that they don't have a notion of a greater Enemy in the same sense as Christians do. Shaitan/Iblis tries to seduce or trick humans into sin, but isn't an enemy to Allah (he's actually a faithful), just jealous, and his role as such is fairly minor. So the notion of a pact with the Devil isn't a thing in Islam.<br /> <br /> On the matter of the Council, I think by this time it is a largely ceremonial division anyways. As an institution the Tremere are still more Mages than Vampires, and in this side they are at war and losing ground, it is still the beginning of the Massassa War, probably still moving all their Chantries to flee their enemies, and even the make-up of the clan may be more of living Mage followers of the Inner Circle than Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T23:13:03-07:00","id":1457692,"title":"","content":"As I vaguely recall in Mage (esp Dark Ages) the Subtle Ones had some significant ties to the Order of Hermes so you could play on those as a bridge for the Tremere. I'm not sure the Tremere proper would tolerate that (except perhaps to use/exploit such a connection) but I wouldn't find it hard for a splinter group of Tremere magi (say a group of mortals and recently turned vampires) who perhaps sought out the Subtle Ones for some reason (and likely pursued by the Tremere proper for their 'betrayal' at that.) I mean if the Telyavelic Tremere can be an offshoot I don't see why another couldn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T00:05:46-07:00","id":1457695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457645-tremere-council-of-seven-spheres-of-control?p=1457648#post1457648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Tremere would be operating (or would want to operate) pretty much wherever the Hermetic mages of Europe previously operated, and slowly expanding from that.<br /> <br /> Therefore, as inspiration I would use the original Tribunals from Ars Magica and slot them in wherever possible.<br /> Using the existing Councilar areas as a starting point, I think this is how things would be:<br /> <br /> Goratrix - &quot;France&quot; likely corresponds to the Tribunals of Normandy and Provencal (Flanders, Burgundy, southern France, the Pyrenees, Provence, Vasconia and western Lombardy).<br /> <br /> Meerlinda - The British Isles would include the old Tribunals of Stonehenge, Loch Legean, and Hibernia which is pretty much what you would expect with the British Isles.<br /> <br /> Abetorius - This would be the Tribunals of Thebes and Levant (corresponding to the possessions of the Byzantine Empire around 800, excluding Italy but including the rest of its European possessions, Asia Minor, the Holy Land &amp; the crusader Kingdoms, the Levant and Egypt).<br /> <br /> Etrius - The Transylvanian Tribunal (non-Byzantine southeastern Europe, Hungary, Bulgaria and Serb and Croat lands).<br /> <br /> Xavier - Iberia corresponds to the Iberian Tribunal which is both Christian and Muslim Spain. I would also think it includes the Roman Tribunal which includes the Italian south of the HRE, Sicily, Sardinia and Corsica, and the Maghreb. This makes for a compact Mediterranean area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks very much for this! Brilliant. A great discussion all around too. Thanks everyone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.obsidianportal.com/campaigns/the-concord-of-ashes\" target=\"_blank\">The Concord of Ashes</a>, my Dark Ages Vampire Chronicle","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1790-haligaunt","name":"Haligaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1790_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T02:04:45-07:00","id":1457697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457645-tremere-council-of-seven-spheres-of-control?p=1457650#post1457650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not an expert, but I believe at this time Islam was quite tolerant during this period. Often it's the case that if you aren't muslim, they'll leave you and your religious practices alone (so long as you pay more tax)<br /> <br /> As for attitudes to magic, there is a real bias. People that make contact with spirits and such? That's Evil and must be punished. But using the stars, alchemy, or other non-blasphemous methods? That's just making use of God's creation. The Tremere really have the most compatible paradigm, and they would really benefit from embracing non-strict muslims. Hermeticism requires some faith but it also requires some flexibility, and for that, the Islamic world at this time is no worse than the Christian one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Islam was quite tolerant towards people of the book, because they were often granted the Dhimmi status. Kafir on the other hand had it pretty bad. And I highly doubt that warlocks would ever be granted the Dhimmi status.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is according to the Quran the doing of the devil. Furthermore blood is something sacred and consuming or doing rituals with it would probably have been seen as a blasphemous act.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T02:37:26-07:00","id":1457698,"title":"","content":"that's more general vampire persecution more than a religious issue.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is a pretty... difficult term. After all, the Scholars of this period contributed towards alchemical and astrological knowledge. Much of Islam's distaste for sorcery really comes from two things; Fear of Idolatry, and also, well, cursing people for selfish reasons isn't very nice. It's very much a matter of High/Low magic. When Tremere conduct rituals, only a few require them to get bloody. Most of it presumably takes the appearance of Alchemy or Astrology. The Tremere appear to be trying to understand God and the world. They're scholars, or at least they could be very good at putting up such a facade. The Islam idea of an evil sorcerer is a disenfranchised, mentally ill bumpkin with a grudge and imaginary friends, a description which matches about half the Assamite Sorcerers. The Tremere don't really fit into that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T04:47:24-07:00","id":1457700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haligaunt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457645-tremere-council-of-seven-spheres-of-control#post1457645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Holy Roman Empire is obvious, but what then of Etrius' interest in Vienna/Austria?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the answer there is that the Holy Roman Empire is overseen by Lotharius. He's already a major figure in the clan as prince of Vienna and was one of the first Tremere Embraced outside of the original seven. The usurpers made lots of enemies during the years from 1022 to 1220 and it feels believable that one or more of the original councilors were destroyed. If anything, it's hard to believe that some of them wouldn't have been. So the next-most senior people got promoted and Etrius was happy to push for his childe being in charge of Tremere interests across the HRE. He knew Lotharius would run things to his satisfaction. I can't see him letting one of Goratrix's allies take over his pet project in Vienna.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what then of Scandinavia, the Baltic, and the Slavic West and North? I seem to recall that he was less than nostalgic about his Scandinavian heritage, but in Clan Novel Tremere, Etrius clearly has an interest in destroying or bringing to heel the Telyavelic Tremere, perhaps implying that he has a loose oversight over the Baltic at least... </div> </div> </div>I could see Scandinavia belonging to Meerlinda. The original seven Tremere were alive when the North Sea Empire was a thing and she might have claimed it on those grounds alone, or Tremere might have simply given it to her because she felt she was up to the task of managing a larger domain. Alternatively, it could be claimed by the councilor of the Holy Roman Empire on the basis of shared Germanic culture. (The Tremere have precedent for that sort of thing with Australia belonging to the councilor of Western Europe in the Modern Nights.) The actual Tremere presence there is probably pretty small either way.<br /> <br /> I could see the Baltic, Slavic West, and Slavic West all belonging to Etrius. He's the closest councilor nearby and the actual Tremere presence in many of them, like Scandinavia, is probably pretty thin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does North Africa get a look-in? </div> </div> </div>I'd make it split between Calderon/Iberia and Abetorius/the Levant.<br /> <br /> Black Fox's tribunals idea is also pretty awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T05:28:06-07:00","id":1457702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457645-tremere-council-of-seven-spheres-of-control?p=1457697#post1457697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcery is according to the Quran the doing of the devil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.<br /> <br /> First, the notion of devil in the Quran is quite different of the notion of devil for Christians. When talking about magic or sorcery it uses the words Shaitan/Shayatin, but in the Quran those words refer to anyone who actively work to lead the faithful astray, for any reason, including common humans. There is no figure of an Ultimate Evil or Source of All Evil there, something isn't evil because it comes from a shaitan, it's that person or djinn in particular that is considered shaitan because they're teaching or encouraging wrong things.<br /> <br /> Also, sorcery is a difficult term as MyWifeIsScary said. Every religion, including the Abrahamic ones, has a history of holy mysticism and magical practices, and most considered magical studies as a form of deepening ones understanding and servitude to God. Solomon is almost universally considered a righteous and faithful practitioner of the magical arts under God's guidance. The idea that we currently translate as &quot;sorcery&quot; is that of magic that subverts God's intents, which is just as nebulous a concept as it seems, so it wasn't interpreted in the same way everywhere and every time.<br /> <br /> In the 13th century most works on philosophy, alchemy, astronomy, mathematics <u>and magic</u> came from the Islamic world, and this more open approach to magic and science will remain pretty much until the mid-20th century, AFAIK, when more extreme religious views gain momentum as a response to European intervention after the fall of the Ottoman Empire in 1922.<br /> <br /> The modern understanding and stance on witchcraft and sorcery only started to take form with the publication of the Malleus Maleficarum in 1483, and only started to get momentum in the 16th century with the &quot;morality wars&quot; between the Protestant Reform and the Roman orthodoxy, which shaped a lot of current popular beliefs on medieval religion, things that weren't medieval to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T12:43:04-07:00","id":1457816,"title":"","content":"I think the Tremere would avoid pushing into the middle east. They have enough enemies, and while they no doubt have a presence in some African and Levant holdings to hunt salubri it is definitely a covert one at the time. After all the Assamites are more then happy to hunt Tremere in that time, especially in territory they know, and the tremere give a variety of reasons to be hunted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T13:58:37-07:00","id":1457821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457645-tremere-council-of-seven-spheres-of-control?p=1457816#post1457816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Tremere would avoid pushing into the middle east. They have enough enemies, and while they no doubt have a presence in some African and Levant holdings to hunt salubri it is definitely a covert one at the time. After all the Assamites are more then happy to hunt Tremere in that time, especially in territory they know, and the tremere give a variety of reasons to be hunted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things to consider. <br /> 1: at this point, very few vampires belong to reaching organizations, and most vampires don't have much interest outside their provinces. The Tremere are one of the very few groups who do organize on a large scale. If the Tremere want a chantry in, say, Naples, the Tremere's enemies aren't going to help much from Rome or Milan, the Vampires in Naples will need to rely on their own efforts, whilst Tremere in Rome or Milan will support a Naples effort with supplies, troops, boons and mortal influence. <br /> <br /> <br /> 2. Vampires can reproduce almost as much as they want. So if our Naples plan ended in a worst case scenario with everybody dead or running, The Tremere can try again and again. This assurance means it's not rea\u013aly a bad idea to try and expand rapidly, at least in vampire terms. <br /> <br /> 3 most Princes are going to know that the Tremere have the Advantage of points 1 and 2, so war is really a bad option. The best they can do is stall. But once a Tremere is in, the Prestation racks up, and eventually there are eight Tremere in a clubhouse and their domain is semi-autonomous and covers a quater of the city. Half the city still owe them debts. <br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah. I change my mind from earlier. The Tremere should expand as fast as possible in every direction. Once each member is trained and indoctrinated, send them out to conquer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T20:51:49-07:00","id":1457859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457645-tremere-council-of-seven-spheres-of-control?p=1457816#post1457816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Tremere would avoid pushing into the middle east. They have enough enemies, and while they no doubt have a presence in some African and Levant holdings to hunt salubri it is definitely a covert one at the time. After all the Assamites are more then happy to hunt Tremere in that time, especially in territory they know, and the tremere give a variety of reasons to be hunted.</div> </div> </div> </div>By 1220 the Tremere have enemies everywhere, and staying where their presence is expected isn't especially worse than entering Banu Haqin territory. Even because the Banu Haqin aren't the only vampires in the Middle East, despite being the only clan distinctly Middle Eastern.<br /> <br /> At this time the Islamic world stretches far and wide. The French Catholics are only beginning to take the Iberian peninsula from the Muslims, who also have control of north Africa and Turkey, effectively controlling most of the Mediterranean coast, barred by the Byzantine from expanding to Europe. It is a center of knowledge and research into the sciences and arts of the time, things that the Tremere have a keen interest on.<br /> <br /> With the Order of Hermes and the Tzimisce hunting them and their main projects for securing their place among the undead starting to get momentum, the Tremere are very likely, in my opinion, to secure at least some positions in the Islamic World, including the Middle East, maybe even trying to strike some sort of peace with the Banu Haqin, maybe offering help in finding a cure for the Baali Curse on the clan.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the Ashirra at the time worked against western incursions, but not necessarily against western migrants if those accepted to live under their laws. And just that, since forced conversions weren't a thing for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T00:57:16-07:00","id":1457875,"title":"","content":"The Tremere at this point don't have any special beef with the Assamites, that comes later when they curse the clan near the formation of the Camarilla. As I've said before, the Tremere have less issues with Islam than the Assamites. Maybe some princes will welcome Tremere in order to check the Assamites. <br /> <br /> The Tremere certainly have a tempting offer. They are simply better at magic than their competitors, and if the Tremere hide their monopolistic intentions for a time, the competition the Tremere offer will lower the price of thaumaturgy. The Tremere seem to be a good deal for the economy, at least so long as you're not a thaumaturge (and princes rarely are, study takes too much time awway from ruling)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}